<title>USA: US corp high-yield fund outflow $663 mln latest wk.</title>
<headline>US corp high-yield fund outflow $663 mln latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash outflows from U.S. corporate high-yield mutual funds totaled $662.8 million in the week ended April 2, according to AMG Data Services.</p>
<p>The number represented the third consecutive negative weekly reading, bringing the total hemorrhage of cash from high-yield bond funds to more than $1.4 billion since March 12, AMG said.  </p>
<p>In addition, outflows have accelerated since turning negative. The latest report follows outflows of $422.8 million and $314.9 million for weeks ending March 26 and March 19, respectively.</p>
<p>Cash flows had been positive for five months.</p>
<p>((--Al Yoon, 212-859-1672))</p>
